        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mechanism_2",
      "name": "grain boundary slip",
      "category": "deformation",
      "sample_id": "sample_1",
      "material_state": "tested at high temperature",
      "assertion_level": "directly_reported",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 2,
          "section": "1. Introduction",
          "quote": "During high-temperature deformation processes in particular, the grain boundary slip mechanism takes precedence.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "e6d070cff4b3e870:part:001"
        },
        {
          "page": "10",
          "section": null,
          "quote": "Consequently, the mechanism of grain boundary slip took precedence during elevated temperature deformation, with grain boundaries prone to microcrack formation due to their inherent weakness [17].",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "e6d070cff4b3e870:part:002"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mechanism_3",
      "name": "dynamic recovery and recrystallization",
      "category": "microstructural",
      "sample_id": "sample_1",
      "material_state": "tested at high temperature",
      "assertion_level": "author_interpretation",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 9,
          "section": "3. Results and Discussions",
          "quote": "Meanwhile, thermally activated dynamic recovery and recrystallization processes occurred, consuming dislocations and decreasing ﬂow stress [43].",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "e6d070cff4b3e870:part:001"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mechanism_4",
      "name": "dynamic recovery",
      "category": "softening",
      "sample_id": "sample_1",
      "material_state": "as-deformed",
      "assertion_level": "directly_reported",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": "10",
          "section": null,
          "quote": "The dynamic softening mechanisms include dynamic recovery, dynamic recrystallization, and insulation heating [45]. Dynamic recovery facilitates the migration and reaction of dislocations, leading to reduced dislocation densities.",
